# The checks branch protection requires on the default branch.
#
# scripts/setup.sh sends every `check` line to GitHub as a required status
# check. scripts/check-required-contexts.sh (part of `make verify`) fails
# when these lines and the pull-request jobs of the `workflow` files
# disagree, in either direction. Add a job to one of these workflows and
# its name goes here in the same pull request.
#
# workflow <path>   a workflow whose pull-request jobs gate merges
# check <name>      a job name, as the job reports it
workflow .github/workflows/ci.yml
workflow .github/workflows/codeql.yml
workflow .github/workflows/security-scan.yml
check build & test (toolchain container)
check portability smoke (macos-latest)
check portability smoke (windows-latest)
check sanitizers (ASan + UBSan)
check thread sanitizer (TSan)
check coverage
check clang-format
check lint workflows and scripts (actionlint + shellcheck)
check static analysis (clang-tidy)
check fuzz smoke (libFuzzer)
check bench smoke (Google Benchmark)
check dependency review
check verify extras (canary, purity, strict, exe, drift)
check container scan (trivy)
check prose
check attribution (no AI credit in commits)
check analyze (c-cpp)
check analyze (actions)
